[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954697970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107295#issuecomment-2954697970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107295","id":2954697970,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wHRzy","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T05:38:49Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T05:44:06Z","body":"Change looks well worth making. Incidentally, I don't know if this would work too, but in a similar library recently I put all these string conversion functions into the `String` class rather than the classes themselves, to avoid bloating the classes with such details.\r\n\r\nNow that it is explicit, would an alternative be a constructor on `String`? :thinking: \r\nI guess the choice is make the classes themselves heavier, or the `String`. There are probably pluses and minuses for both.\r\n\r\n```\r\nclass Vector3;\r\n\r\nclass String\r\n{\r\npublic:\r\n\texplicit String(int64_t p_value);\r\n\texplicit String(const Vector3 &p_value);\r\n\t...etc\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2954697970/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2955141006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107295#issuecomment-2955141006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107295","id":2955141006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wI9-O","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-09T09:00:16Z","updated_at":"2025-06-09T09:00:28Z","body":"> Now that it is explicit, would an alternative be a constructor on String? 🤔\n\nThis is possible, whether they're explicit or implicit.\n\nThe main question is which of the types the string conversion binds more tightly to. I'd say `String` is the more fundamental type compared to any of these math types, so it should not be including them or handling string conversions for them. But i could see other peo